{
    "background_story": "Aaron was a young Jewish boy living in Berlin during the rise of Nazism in the 1930s. As the Nazi party's grip on Germany tightened, Aaron's family faced increasing persecution. Despite the danger, Aaron's father, a prominent rabbi, continued to speak out against the Nazi regime. In 1938, Aaron's family was forced to flee their home after Kristallnacht, the Night of Broken Glass. They made their way to the Netherlands, where they lived in hiding for several years. Aaron's experiences during this time had a profound impact on him, and he became determined to fight against injustice and oppression. He joined the Dutch resistance, using his skills to help smuggle Jews to safety and disrupt Nazi operations. After the war, Aaron dedicated his life to sharing the lessons of the Holocaust, ensuring that the atrocities committed by the Nazi regime would never be forgotten.",
